From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: branch init by saved EPC

The physical SF2000 log for the one-shot identity-init image still stops at
the final restore marker. The retained header reports marker 0x51510001 and a
post-RESTORE_SOME CP0 status without ERL, so the ERL-bit test skips the copied
identity stub even though the saved pt_regs status was prepared for the first
/init handoff.

Key the special branch off the saved /init EPC instead. That value is the
handoff target we need to intercept and it is still available in pt_regs at the
restore point. Mark this branch decision as 0x51510007; if the copied stub
runs it will still overwrite the marker with 0x51510006 before jumping to
/init.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -149,12 +149,12 @@ restore_partial:		# restore partial frame
 	MFC0	k1, CP0_EPC
 	sw	k1, 28(k0)
 	sync
-	LONG_L	k1, PT_STATUS(sp)
-	andi	k1, ST0_ERL
-	beqz	k1, 1f
+	LONG_L	k1, PT_EPC(sp)
+	li	k0, 0x004002f0
+	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
-	li	k1, 0x51510003
+	li	k1, 0x51510007
 	sw	k1, 20(k0)
 	LONG_L	k1, PT_R29(sp)
 	sw	k1, 24(k0)
-- 
2.45.0
